From 4b597d28345354dff31655ee57ec6ec5212f968c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 21:12:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09360/11362] Fix nine adversarial-review findings in the
 compaction carried state

Follow-up to d3e9f8cf52. An adversarial review found nine issues. Two were
confirmed independently before any fix was written, and the highest-severity fix
is proven by mutation rather than asserted.

The tail carried the wrong turn. `rebuild_messages` started the tail at the last
assistant turn of any kind, but the design says the last assistant TOOL-CALL
turn, and marks the last tool round "verbatim tail, never compacted". When the
threshold-crossing reply was prose, the rebuild produced four messages with no
tool result in them, and the mismatch report the model was about to act on
collapsed to a 240-character digest. The scan now requires `tool_calls`, and
everything after that turn is carried, because a trailing prose turn and an
unanswered nudge are part of the same reasoning step.

The spec had been softened to match the code. It said "the last assistant turn",
so spec and code agreed while both drifted from the design they cite. That is
worse than a plain bug: it removes the signal that anything is wrong. The spec
now states the tool-call rule, and the design note records the softening as an
implementation defect rather than a decision.

Five guard conditions were decorative. Deleting each left the suite green,
including the check that failed tool calls are not evidence, whose absence makes
a failed submission poison the duplicate counter for a later identical success.
Each now has a test proven by applying the mutation, watching the new test go
red, restoring, and watching it go green.

Compaction could thrash at default knobs. A tail round near 6k tokens re-fired
every turn, forfeiting the prefix-cache benefit that justifies triggering on a
threshold at all. A re-fire now requires fresh transcript growth beyond the first
post-rebuild measurement. The floor is the brake; the alarm above five events is
the backstop.

Also: refetch keys derive from the tool RESULT, so tool-side defaults and
clipping normalize instead of under-counting the "digest too lossy" signal; goal
probes join the eviction order; a keep-set that alone busts the budget ships
whole rather than destroying recoverable evidence for no gain; the consecutive
user messages every rebuild emits are documented and a transport failure on the
first post-rebuild request is now distinguishable; float token counts coerce
instead of silently disabling the trigger; and the sizing and shipping
serializers agree.

64 tests pass, up from 51. The env-unset byte-identity pin passes unchanged
against all of it, and the env var still appears nowhere outside its own module
and tests. No default flipped.

